summary:
- topic: Start of School Year Update
  text: The Superintendent provided a comprehensive update on the start of the 2026-2027
    school year, highlighting summer projects like secure vestibules at Skillin and
    Dyer, the relocation of Kaler staff, and the onboarding of new leadership. The
    report also covered the successful launch of the new cell phone policy at secondary
    schools, with the administration addressing parent safety concerns.
- topic: 'Public Comment: School Board Candidates'
  text: A significant portion of public comment was dedicated to candidates running
    for at-large school board seats. Stephanie Edwards, Carl Parsons, and Ishmeel
    Daniels introduced themselves, outlining their platforms which included fiscal
    responsibility, teacher retention, transparency, and long-term planning.
- topic: 'Public Comment: Community Concerns'
  text: Citizens raised concerns about bullying prevention, the need for a later middle
    school start time, the accuracy of district surveys, and the safety of portables.
    Several speakers also addressed the upcoming elementary reconfiguration and the
    district's budget.
- topic: FY26 Budget Closeout and Fund Balance
  text: The Finance Committee reported that the district is projected to close the
    FY26 budget with only a ~$1,000 deficit, a significant improvement from earlier
    projections. However, this leaves the district with virtually no fund balance,
    a situation Member Richardson and several public commenters described as concerning
    and irresponsible, especially with potential facility emergencies looming.
- topic: 'Policy Updates: Cell Phones and Public Participation'
  text: The board unanimously passed the second read of the new rules for personal
    electronic devices, formalizing the 'away for the day' policy. They also held
    a first read for changes to the public participation policy (BEDH), which proposes
    eliminating the practice of yielding time to other speakers and setting a 10:00
    PM meeting end time, sparking debate during public comment.
- topic: Committee Reports
  text: The Buildings & Grounds Committee reported on progress with the middle school
    solar array, contingency planning for the aging Skillin Elementary boiler, and
    the design phase for the South Portland High School Athletic Complex. The Policy
    Committee advanced the cell phone and public participation policies.
